<!-- FAQ Section -->
<section id="faq" class="section-container">
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-kicker">Engineering FAQ</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4 class="faq-question">What is included in the free trial?</h4>
        <p class="faq-answer">
          14 days and 30 verified questions, with one MySQL connection. You get SQL Studio, API keys, and the same read-only engine as paid plans. No credit card. When the trial ends or the 30 questions are used, subscribe to the plan that matches your schema.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4 class="faq-question">Can Querywell modify, update, or drop tables?</h4>
        <p class="faq-answer">
          Querywell keeps access read-only in two places. The connection probe checks database grants and confirms writes fail before credentials are saved. Generated SQL is limited to <code>SELECT</code> statements.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4 class="faq-question">Do our customer rows leave our database?</h4>
        <p class="faq-answer">
          Querywell indexes metadata only: table names, column names, data types, foreign keys, and short categorical lookup values such as status codes. Business rows are queried at runtime and returned to the browser. They are not saved in Querywell.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4 class="faq-question">Can we connect Querywell to a read replica?</h4>
        <p class="faq-answer">
          Yes. A read replica is the recommended production setup. MySQL on Aurora, RDS, or Cloud SQL keeps query load off the primary write node.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4 class="faq-question">What happens if our database schema changes?</h4>
        <p class="faq-answer">
          You can re-index your schema at any time with a single click in the <strong>Database Source</strong> tab. Re-indexing takes 2 to 10 seconds depending on schema size.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4 class="faq-question">Can we call Querywell from our own app?</h4>
        <p class="faq-answer">
          Yes. Create an API key, then <code>POST /api/ask</code> with the question. The JSON response includes the generated SQL and the rows. See the <a href="/docs">Ask API docs</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
